Subject: Keep PHP's pointers and capabilities intact under Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Fil-C traps on inline assembly it cannot prove safe. Take Zend's existing
portable paths for string comparison (memcmp) and zend_safe_address, spell
xgetbv as the instruction Fil-C lowers instead of raw opcode bytes, and drop
the gdb helper scripts embedded with module assembly in .debug_gdb_scripts.

Fil-C also drops a pointer's capability when the pointer becomes an integer.
Weak references tag their payload pointers through uintptr_t, and WeakMap
keys are object addresses shifted into integers; tag with pointer arithmetic
and recover key objects from a weak exact pointer table, which keeps the
integer values. Typed-property references tag their source list through the
integer member of a union; make that member a pointer.

Fil-C runs a ucontext fiber on a native stack its runtime allocates, so
Zend's stack limit for a fiber is measured from the fiber's first frame
instead of from the memory PHP allocated for it.

